---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ContentSection from '../../components/ContentSection.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import LinkCard from '../../components/LinkCard.astro';

const relatedPages = [
  { title: 'College Basketball Hub', href: '/college-basketball-betting', description: 'Complete CBB guide' },
  { title: 'March Madness', href: '/college-basketball/march-madness-betting', description: 'Tournament betting' },
  { title: 'How Odds Work', href: '/how-betting-odds-work', description: 'Understanding odds' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="College Basketball Live Betting Guide"
  description="In-game betting for college basketball, pace adjustments, foul trouble opportunities, and when live wagering might offer value."
>
  <Hero
    title="College Basketball Live Betting"
    subtitle="In-Game Wagering for College Hoops"
    size="medium"
  />

  <div class="container content-container">
    <article class="page-content">
      <ContentSection>
        <div class="quick-take">
          <h2>Quick Take</h2>
          <p>
            College basketball's high-variance nature creates dramatic in-game swings that live betting markets try to price in real-time. Runs of 10-15 points happen frequently, temporarily distorting spreads. While these swings create apparent opportunities, the market adjusts quickly, and most "value" you think you see is already priced in. Live betting CBB requires extreme selectivity and fast action.
          </p>
        </div>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="What Makes CBB Live Betting Different?" id="differences">
        <h3>High scoring variance</h3>
        <p>
          College basketball features frequent scoring runs. A 12-0 run can flip a 10-point lead into a 2-point deficit in three minutes. These swings create volatile live lines.
        </p>

        <h3>Foul trouble matters more</h3>
        <p>
          With five fouls to disqualification and often limited bench depth, key players in foul trouble significantly impacts game flow. Live lines adjust when starters go to the bench.
        </p>

        <h3>Pace variation</h3>
        <p>
          College games vary more in pace than NBA. A slow-paced game might not reach projected totals; a tempo push can blow through them. Live totals require pace awareness.
        </p>

        <h3>Less sophisticated markets</h3>
        <p>
          While major conference games have sharp live markets, mid-major and lower-profile games may have less efficient live pricing—though also lower limits and more risk.
        </p>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="When Might Live Betting Offer Opportunities?" id="opportunities">
        <Callout type="warning" title="Most Opportunities Are Mirages">
          <p>
            What looks like a slow adjustment is usually already priced in. The book's algorithm knows about the scoring run before you've processed it.
          </p>
        </Callout>

        <h3>Foul trouble on key players</h3>
        <p>
          If a team's star picks up their second foul in the first five minutes and goes to the bench, the live line adjusts. If you believe the market overreacted (or underreacted), there may be opportunity—but you need to be fast and confident.
        </p>

        <h3>Pace mismatches playing out</h3>
        <p>
          If your pre-game analysis included pace considerations and the game is confirming your thesis, live totals might offer continuation bets.
        </p>

        <h3>Blowout deceleration</h3>
        <p>
          Games that become blowouts often slow down significantly. The winning team slows pace; the losing team may concede. Live spreads in garbage time can overcorrect.
        </p>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="What This Means for Bettors" id="what-means">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Have a thesis before the game:</strong> Know what you're looking for so you can act quickly when you see it.</li>
          <li><strong>Accept that most games don't offer live value:</strong> Passing is usually correct.</li>
          <li><strong>Don't chase:</strong> If your pre-game bet is losing, don't try to fix it live.</li>
          <li><strong>Set strict limits:</strong> Decide your live betting budget before the game starts.</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Common Misconceptions" id="misconceptions">
        <h3>A 15-2 run means the trailing team is due</h3>
        <p>
          Momentum is a narrative, not a predictive force. The team that just went on a run might continue dominating.
        </p>

        <h3>I can react faster than the book</h3>
        <p>
          Sportsbooks have algorithms processing the game faster than human perception. Your information advantage is minimal.
        </p>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Key Takeaways" id="takeaways">
        <ul>
          <li>CBB live betting features high variance due to scoring runs</li>
          <li>Foul trouble and pace changes create the most notable line movements</li>
          <li>Markets adjust quickly—apparent opportunities often aren't</li>
          <li>Extreme selectivity is required for profitable live betting</li>
          <li>Never chase losses mid-game</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Related Resources" id="related">
        <div class="related-grid">
          {relatedPages.map((page) => (
            <LinkCard title={page.title} href={page.href} description={page.description} />
          ))}
        </div>
      </ContentSection>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-content { padding: var(--spacing-3xl) 0; }
  .quick-take { background-color: var(--color-surface); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent); padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: 0 var(--border-radius) var(--border-radius) 0; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl); }
  .quick-take h2 { font-size: 1rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--color-accent); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); }
  .quick-take p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .related-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--spacing-md); margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); }
  @media (max-width: 768px) { .related-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
